IMPORT prelude

-- Misuse of Drugs Act 1973 (Singapore) -- what I can be charged with, what the court will presume against me, and whether I must
-- give a urine specimen.
--
-- SEAT: the person suspected of, or charged with, a drug offence (the accused person). Every decision is phrased as that person
-- would ask it, on facts that person could state.
--
-- Provisions covered: s 2 ("traffic"), ss 5, 6, 7, 8 (which offence an act falls under), s 8A (consumption abroad), ss 17, 18, 21,
-- 22 (presumptions), s 31(1), (2), (4) (urine specimens and the offence of failing to give one).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, version in force from 1/6/2026, as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/MDA1973.txt (SSO, retrieved 2026-10-01).
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the First, Third, Fourth and Fifth Schedules (which substances are controlled drugs, their class, which drugs are
-- "specified drugs", excluded substances) -- these are asked as facts; Part 2A (psychoactive substances, ss 11F to 11Q) except where
-- a previous conviction under it is an input to punishment; ss 9 to 11E, 12 to 14; the presumptions in ss 19 and 20; the
-- certificates (ss 15, 16); search, arrest and seizure (ss 24 to 30); hair and oral fluid tests (ss 31A, 31B); the Director's
-- urine-test orders under s 31(1A) and the Armed Forces power in s 31(1B); s 31(3) (non-citizens arriving); Part 4 (treatment and
-- rehabilitation); committees of inquiry; regulations and the Schedules-amending power. Punishment is in mda-punishment.l4.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the individual to
-- whom the law is applied, with the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass,
-- no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Misuse of Drugs Act 1973 -- offences and presumptions`

-- The drugs the Act names by name in ss 17 and the Second Schedule. Any other controlled drug is `another controlled drug`; whether
-- a substance is a controlled drug at all, and its class, is the First Schedule's question and is asked as a fact.
DECLARE Drug IS ONE OF
    opium                                                   -- s 2: morphine with codeine, narcotine, papaverine or thebaine
    morphine
    diamorphine                                             -- (heroin; gloss, not the Act's word)
    cannabis                                                -- s 2: any part of a plant of the genus Cannabis
    `cannabis mixture`                                      -- s 2: vegetable matter containing THC and cannabinol
    `cannabis resin`
    cocaine
    methamphetamine
    ketamine
    `one of the three phenethylamines in section 17(i)`     -- named in the Act by chemical name only
    `another controlled drug`

§§ `2, 5, 6, 7, 8 -- which offence my act is`

-- s 2: "traffic" means "(a) to sell, give, administer, transport, send, deliver or distribute; or (b) to offer to do anything
-- mentioned in paragraph (a), otherwise than under the authority of this Act".
-- s 5(1): an offence "(a) to traffic in a controlled drug; (b) to offer to traffic ...; or (c) to do or offer to do any act
-- preparatory to or for the purpose of trafficking". (2): "a person commits the offence of trafficking in a controlled drug if he or
-- she has in his or her possession that drug for the purpose of trafficking".
-- s 6: to manufacture. s 7: "to import into or export from Singapore". s 8: "(a) have in his or her possession a controlled drug; or
-- (b) smoke, administer to himself or herself or otherwise consume" one. Each opens "Except as authorised by this Act".
DECLARE `My act` IS ONE OF
    `I sold it`
    `I gave it to someone`
    `I administered it to someone else`
    `I transported it`
    `I sent it`
    `I delivered it`
    `I distributed it`
    `I offered to do one of those things`
    `I did an act preparatory to trafficking it`
    `I had it for the purpose of trafficking`
    `I had it for my own use`
    `I consumed it myself`
    `I brought it into or took it out of Singapore`
    `I made it`

DECLARE `Drug offence` IS ONE OF
    `trafficking, section 5`
    `manufacture, section 6`
    `import or export, section 7`
    `possession, section 8(a)`
    `consumption, section 8(b)`
    `no offence, because the act was authorised under this Act`

-- Inference, labelled: an act that is trafficking under s 5(2) is also possession; the encoding names the section the text pins
-- the act to, not every offence it may also be.
GIVEN `my act` IS A `My act`, `the act was authorised under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Drug offence`
DECIDE `What offence would my act be` IS
    IF `the act was authorised under this Act`
    THEN `no offence, because the act was authorised under this Act`
    ELSE CONSIDER `my act`
         WHEN `I had it for my own use`                       THEN `possession, section 8(a)`
         WHEN `I consumed it myself`                          THEN `consumption, section 8(b)`
         WHEN `I brought it into or took it out of Singapore` THEN `import or export, section 7`
         WHEN `I made it`                                     THEN `manufacture, section 6`
         OTHERWISE                                                 `trafficking, section 5`

§§ `8A, 22, 31(4) -- urine tests`

-- s 31(4): a specimen is divided into 3 parts: "(a) a preliminary urine test must be conducted on one part" and "(b) each of the
-- remaining 2 parts ... must be marked and sealed and a urine test must be conducted on each part by a different person".
DECLARE `My urine test results` IS ONE OF
    `negative on the preliminary test`
    `positive on the preliminary test only`
    `positive on only one of the two sealed parts`
    `positive on both sealed parts`

GIVEN `my results` IS A `My urine test results`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `both of my section 31(4)(b) tests found the drug` IF
    CONSIDER `my results`
    WHEN `positive on both sealed parts` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 22: "If any controlled drug ... is found in the urine of a person as a result of both urine tests conducted under
-- section 31(4)(b), he or she is presumed, until the contrary is proved, to have consumed that controlled drug ... in contravention
-- of section 8(b)".
GIVEN `my results` IS A `My urine test results`, `I prove I did not consume it in contravention of section 8(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I presumed to have consumed the drug` IF
        `both of my section 31(4)(b) tests found the drug` `my results`
    AND NOT `I prove I did not consume it in contravention of section 8(b)`

-- s 8A(1): s 8(b) "has effect in relation to a person who is a citizen of Singapore or a permanent resident of Singapore outside as
-- well as within Singapore where he or she is found as a result of urine tests conducted under section 31(4)(b)" to have consumed;
-- (2) "may be dealt with as if that offence had been committed within Singapore".
GIVEN `I am a citizen or permanent resident of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `my results` IS A `My urine test results`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I be charged in Singapore for consuming a drug abroad` IF
        `I am a citizen or permanent resident of Singapore`
    AND `both of my section 31(4)(b) tests found the drug` `my results`

§§ `17 -- presumed to be trafficking`

-- s 17: "Any person who is proved to have had in his or her possession more than" the quantity below, "whether or not contained in
-- any substance, extract, preparation or mixture, is presumed to have had that drug in possession for the purpose of trafficking
-- unless it is proved that his or her possession of that drug was not for that purpose". The threshold is "more than", so the
-- figure itself does not trigger it. The statutory table, as data:
GIVEN `the drug` IS A Drug
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the section 17 threshold in grammes` IS
    CONSIDER `the drug`
    WHEN opium                                                 THEN JUST 100     -- (a)
    WHEN morphine                                              THEN JUST 3       -- (b)
    WHEN diamorphine                                           THEN JUST 2       -- (c)
    WHEN cannabis                                              THEN JUST 15      -- (d)
    WHEN `cannabis mixture`                                    THEN JUST 30      -- (e)
    WHEN `cannabis resin`                                      THEN JUST 10      -- (f)
    WHEN cocaine                                               THEN JUST 3       -- (g)
    WHEN methamphetamine                                       THEN JUST 25      -- (h)
    WHEN ketamine                                              THEN JUST 113     -- (ha)
    WHEN `one of the three phenethylamines in section 17(i)`   THEN JUST 10      -- (i), "any or any combination"
    OTHERWISE NOTHING                                                            -- s 17 names no other drug

-- s 17 is triggered by possession that is "proved". s 18(2), by contrast, runs from possession "proved or presumed". Inference,
-- labelled: the difference in wording means a possession that is only presumed under s 18(1) does not trigger s 17; the encoding
-- asks whether possession was proved.
GIVEN `the drug` IS A Drug
      `grammes I had` IS A NUMBER
      `my possession is proved, not merely presumed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I prove my possession was not for trafficking` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I presumed to have had the drug for trafficking` IF
        `my possession is proved, not merely presumed`
    AND CONSIDER `the section 17 threshold in grammes` `the drug`
        WHEN JUST threshold THEN `grammes I had` GREATER THAN threshold
        WHEN NOTHING        THEN FALSE
    AND NOT `I prove my possession was not for trafficking`

§§ `18, 21 -- presumed to possess, presumed to know`

-- s 18(1): a person "proved to have had in his or her possession or custody or under his or her control -- (a) anything containing a
-- controlled drug; (b) the keys of anything containing a controlled drug; (c) the keys of any place or premises ... in which a
-- controlled drug is found; or (d) a document of title relating to a controlled drug or any other document intended for the
-- delivery of a controlled drug, is presumed, until the contrary is proved, to have had that drug in his or her possession".
-- (3): the presumptions "are not to be rebutted by proof that the accused never had physical possession".
-- (4): "Where one of 2 or more persons with the knowledge and consent of the rest has any controlled drug in his or her possession,
-- it is deemed to be in the possession of each and all of them" -- deemed, so no rebuttal is provided.
DECLARE `What I had` IS ONE OF
    `something containing the drug`
    `the keys of something containing the drug`
    `the keys of a place where the drug was found`
    `a document of title to the drug, or for its delivery`
    `none of those things`

GIVEN `what I had` IS A `What I had`
      `another of us had the drug with my knowledge and consent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I prove I did not possess it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my only proof is that I never physically held it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I taken to possess the drug` IF
        `another of us had the drug with my knowledge and consent`
    OR  (    `a section 18(1) link`
         AND NOT `rebutted`)
    WHERE
        `a section 18(1) link` MEANS
            CONSIDER `what I had`
            WHEN `none of those things` THEN FALSE
            OTHERWISE TRUE
        `rebutted` MEANS
                `I prove I did not possess it`
            AND NOT `my only proof is that I never physically held it`

-- s 18(2): "Any person who is proved or presumed to have had a controlled drug in his or her possession is presumed, until the
-- contrary is proved, to have known the nature of that drug."
GIVEN `my possession is proved or presumed` IS A BOOLEAN, `I prove I did not know the nature of the drug` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I presumed to have known what the drug was` IF
    `my possession is proved or presumed` AND NOT `I prove I did not know the nature of the drug`

-- s 21: a controlled drug "found in any vehicle ... is presumed, until the contrary is proved, to be in the possession of the owner
-- of the vehicle and of the person in charge of the vehicle for the time being".
GIVEN `I own the vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN, `I was in charge of the vehicle at the time` IS A BOOLEAN, `I prove the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I presumed to possess a drug found in a vehicle` IF
    (`I own the vehicle` OR `I was in charge of the vehicle at the time`) AND NOT `I prove the contrary`

§§ `31(1), (2) -- must I give a urine specimen`

-- s 31(1): "Any officer of the Bureau, immigration officer or police officer not below the rank of sergeant may, if he or she
-- reasonably suspects any person to have committed an offence under section 8(b) or 11I(1)(b), require that person to provide a
-- specimen of the person's urine". (2): "A person who, without reasonable excuse, fails to provide a specimen of his or her urine
-- within such time as may be required by any of the officers ... shall be guilty of an offence."
-- Reading taken, labelled: "not below the rank of sergeant" is read as qualifying the police officer only.
DECLARE `Who asked me` IS ONE OF
    `an officer of the Central Narcotics Bureau`
    `an immigration officer`
    `a police officer of the rank of sergeant or above`
    `a police officer below the rank of sergeant`
    `someone else`

GIVEN `who asked me` IS A `Who asked me`
      `the officer reasonably suspects me of consuming a controlled drug or psychoactive substance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I give a urine specimen when asked` IF
        `the officer reasonably suspects me of consuming a controlled drug or psychoactive substance`
    AND CONSIDER `who asked me`
        WHEN `an officer of the Central Narcotics Bureau`          THEN TRUE
        WHEN `an immigration officer`                              THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a police officer of the rank of sergeant or above`  THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `who asked me` IS A `Who asked me`
      `the officer reasonably suspects me of consuming a controlled drug or psychoactive substance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I gave it within the time the officer required` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I commit an offence by not giving a urine specimen` IF
        `Must I give a urine specimen when asked` `who asked me` `the officer reasonably suspects me of consuming a controlled drug or psychoactive substance`
    AND NOT `I gave it within the time the officer required`
    AND NOT `I had a reasonable excuse`

-- The same duty as a regulative rule: the deadline is "such time as may be required by" the officer, an input.
DECLARE `Party to a urine test` IS ONE OF `I`, `the officer`
DECLARE `Urine test act` IS ONE OF `provide a urine specimen`

GIVEN `the time the officer requires` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party to a urine test` `Urine test act`
DECIDE `my duty to provide a urine specimen` IS
    PARTY  `I`
    MUST   `provide a urine specimen`
    WITHIN `the time the officer requires`
    HENCE  FULFILLED
    LEST   BREACH BY `I`
